      "document": {
        "schema_version": 1,
        "decision": "APPROVE",
        "reviewer": "Claude Code CLI 2.1.317",
        "actual_model": [
          "glm-5.3[1m]"
        ],
        "reviewed_implementation": "3e4c992b444480071100fbd1fb9ea3f8717320c9",
        "reviewed_evidence_commit": "812bad80b0c215b42936445f5a507b183e48dcb5",
        "read_only_inline_evidence": true,
        "result": "**APPROVE** — no concrete blockers. Closure is justified for the stated scope only (P11 fixed-window, isolated provider, E3/E4 smoke).\n\nChecked against the receipts:\n\n- **Sample counts** — internally consistent everywhere: train 589944 rows → 583700 accepted (= fit_samples rows; 589944 − 6244 non-finite labels, matching DropnaLabel at fit), valid 138093 → 137826 (−267), test 106005 = 104859 kept + 1146 cross/undefined → 104772 accepted. README table IC/RankIC values match acceptance.json/run-receipt.json to full precision.\n- **Independent recompute** — `verify_p11_host.py` re-derives the mask from the calendar (T+1/T+2 in-segment, position+2 < len) without importing production mask code, asserts all three mask columns equal, recomputes pooled Pearson/Spearman at 1e-12 tolerance, re-hashes every parquet; `independent_mask_and_metrics_match: true` per segment.\n- **Nominal vs effective** — ends 2024-12-27 / 2025-12-29 are the correct last sessions whose T+2 close stays in-segment (Dec 30/31 2024 and Dec 30/31 2025 cross boundaries); test kept nominal with cross-boundary rows excluded; `all_label_dates_in_nominal_segment: true`; ZScoreNorm fit confined to nominal train (backward-looking features only — no label leakage, and disclosed).\n- **Provider immutability** — all 11406 manifest fingerprints re-verified post-training, protected anchors before/after unchanged, anchors re-hashed against the receipt; the 8 changed live-lake files are documented separately without conflating the frozen provider with the current lake.\n- **CRLF/Git hash accounting** — runtime CRLF hash (`a8b1f1…`) and Git blob hash (`1458e9…`) recorded as distinct values with `source_equal_after_lf_normalization: true`, asserted by the verifier; published-byte vs local-original vs runtime hashes explicitly separated in `validation.json` + `publication-sha256.json`.\n- **Limits** — correctly bounded: pooled metrics explicitly not profitability/daily-IC evidence, old IC retained as historical only, survivorship/front-adjust biases retained, no current-lake refresh, no default-provider promotion, no market writes/QMT/trading; P12/QL11 and model comparison explicitly not closed. Boundary-purge defect is honestly documented via `boundary-before.json` rather than papered over."
      }
    },
